{
  "schema": 1,
  "name": "Maximum Power extends Skirmish even when Elven Tactics skips consuming Advantage (#10207)",
  "contract": [
    "Maximum Power (560688): 'Abilities used with 5 stacks of Advantage now refresh the duration of your active",
    "Skirmish by 5 sec' (560689, SPELL_EFFECT_ASCENSION_MODIFY_AURA_DURATION, misc 802039, +5000 ms, additive to",
    "the aura's current remaining duration). Elven Tactics (560701) adds a flat -20 SPELLMOD_CHANCE_OF_SUCCESS to",
    "Advantage Decrement Passive (582770), giving a probabilistic chance to not consume Advantage on a 5-stack",
    "cast. In HandleAscensionClassMechanicsCast, Maximum Power's extension call used to live inside the",
    "'roll_chance_f(consumeChance) succeeded' branch, so a no-consume roll (Elven Tactics triggering) skipped the",
    "extension even though the ability was still used at 5 stacks; the fix moved the check out of that branch.",
    "Skirmish (802039) itself requires caster aura 804329 (CasterAuraSpell) like other Advantage-gated abilities,",
    "is self-targeted (no miss roll) and recastable, so the fixture resets Advantage to 5 stacks and recasts it",
    "40 times to exercise the consume roll repeatedly without any external-target miss chance.",
    "Extension casts (560689, triggered) and Decrement casts (520618, triggered) are both counted with",
    "spell_cast_count. Under the bug, the extension can only ever fire together with a successful decrement, so",
    "ExtensionCount <= DecrementCount always; the fix makes the extension fire on every 5-stack use while",
    "Skirmish and Maximum Power are active, so ExtensionCount > DecrementCount as soon as a single no-consume",
    "roll lands among the 40 attempts (independent 20% per-cast chance; 40 trials leave well under a tenth of a",
    "percent chance of no such roll)."
  ],
  "timeout_ms": 150000,
  "players": [
    {
      "id": "ranger",
      "race": 1,
      "class": 21,
      "level": 60
    }
  ],
